      "content": "It feels like you're saying we should just accept these vulnerabilities because the alternative is too much trouble. But if a system has known weaknesses that could be exploited, isn't it more \"honest\" to admit that the integrity of the election could be compromised? Why is it more important to protect the \"image\" of the system than to actually address the possibility that it's being manipulated?",
